/* =============================================================================
   ORACLE PASSWORD-EXPIRY EMAIL NOTIFICATIONS
   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   What it does
     - Runs daily at 07:00 America/Chicago via DBMS_SCHEDULER
     - Emails each user whose password expires in <= 14, 7, 3, 1 days,
       and once more if the account is in its grace period
     - Never emails the same user twice for the same threshold (logged)
     - Catches up automatically if a run is missed (weekend, outage)
     - Sends the DBA team a daily summary: who was emailed, service accounts
       nearing expiry, users with no email on file, send failures, and
       accounts that have already fully expired
     - Emails contain no links and no passwords (phishing-safe)

   Requirements
     - Oracle 12.2+ (18c+ for NO AUTHENTICATION schema; see note in Step 1)
     - An SMTP relay reachable from the DB server (plain SMTP, usually port 25)
     - Run as SYS or a DBA account, in SQL*Plus / SQLcl / SQL Developer /
       Toad (Execute as Script, F5)

   IMPORTANT FOR PRODUCTION
     - Run this through change control, test in DEV/TEST first.
     - Granting UTL_SMTP / UTL_TCP and a network ACL to a schema may need
       security / ISSO approval (STIG-related). Document it.

   Sections
     0. Settings              (EDIT THESE)
     1. Schema + privileges   (SYS/DBA)
     2. Network ACL           (SYS/DBA)
     3. Tables
     4. Seed data             (EDIT: profiles, contacts)
     5. Package
     6. Test (dry run, redirect)
     7. Scheduler job
     8. Monitoring queries
     9. Rollback
   ============================================================================= */

SET DEFINE ON
SET SERVEROUTPUT ON SIZE UNLIMITED

